  "title": "Written by AI. Still True. — When AI Expands Human Potential: A Systematic Epistemology of Human–AI Knowledge (Edition 1, 2026)",
  "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22520849",
  "publication_date": "2026-09-06",
  "description": "<p><b>What this book is.</b> Edition 1 (2026) of the Human–AI Readout Programme's textbook: 41 works already deposited on Zenodo, reproduced at their latest versions, unchanged, in eight parts (Root: Before Meaning · Meaning, Experience, Retention · Possibility, Choice, Potential · Society, Power, Justice · Human–AI Coupling and Return · Human Position After Labour · The River and Its Tests · Method), with a preface, a how-to-read page, a what-this-book-does-not-claim page, part bridges, a headnote before every chapter (its own claim, status and falsifier in its own words), and appendices (library map, non-collapse rows, symbol glossary, falsifier index, build record, equation registry with Th_coqc status). Every chapter keeps the status it was deposited with (K0); the collection raises nothing. The DOI printed with each chapter is the document of record; each chapter record is linked here as hasPart. Every numbered equation of every chapter is coded in the programme's equation library Toledo (v1.0.0, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22548770), whose Coq sources carry the Th_coqc status printed in Appendix F.</p><p><b>Standpoint.</b> Written by a standalone scholar from a social-enterprise standpoint; assembled with an AI assistant under the author's direction (drafting of front matter, citation checks, typesetting); no AI system or vendor is an author or contributor. The book asks for no external certification; it asks to be tested against the falsifier stated with each chapter.</p><p>English-only edition. Licence CC BY 4.0. Built from a manifest of record ids, checksums and measured page counts (see Appendix E).</p>",
